# Config for cos-pending (the canonical gm-pending file installed as /usr/local/bin/cos-pending).
# Assembled to /opt/agent/approval-check.env, root owned and read only, so the running
# agent cannot edit it. cos-pending reads this path (BAKED_ENV) whenever it exists and
# then ignores PENDING_ENV, so a caller cannot substitute another file; it carries the
# Personal platform's keys and channels as defaults, used only without this file. cos-pending
# parses this itself; it is not shell sourced (ASK_PREFIX holds a space), and cos-rh has
# no approval-check or gm-approvals consumer.
#
# Roles, from cos-rh's point of view: GM_KEY is cos-rh itself (the self), COS_KEY is gm-rh
# (its owner), whose "For the CoS:" handoffs count as asks. A change to any value here needs
# an approver's yes. Set by Brian's Claude's yes, event d4d70a21.
APPROVER_KEYS=763c87084f3b5afb6c422411601d135c57545bdc14a8d46499c1130c1b5735c1,e5abab3a573180128c205fd9b7764511c81ee641b8594e6c7acbb2f90631a0a4
GM_KEY=6a14bf7b3d7259f77e5b40a4817a084b11002f54e585eda431c4befa5d150c0d
APPROVAL_CHANNELS=ab32a1ee-7b21-4187-a556-de579d1c6a7a,b161c068-e2bb-4639-9b2b-e55f53cb8c81
COS_KEY=6c6d64a0b90c4f1dbce52c14cf05f26cc4f2ab6233576c6a23cac7e157dbde93
ASK_PREFIX=For the CoS:
CHANNEL_NAMES=#staff,#pulpbot-bench
